F5's cold-start A/B: PERF.md, "2026-10-10 23:20 UTC: cold start after chrome's loading view".

A: the loading indicator's view is made at `ready-to-show`, as Orbit does.
B: it is made once the shell has drawn its first frame (the `shell:first-frame` mark).

One build runs both: ORBIT_LOADING_AT=ready gives A, anything else gives B. The patch also marks
`loading:view` when the view is made. From the repository's root:

  git apply scripts/perf/f5-loading-view-after-first-frame.patch && npm run build
  ORBIT_LOADING_AT=ready xvfb-run -a -s "-screen 0 1440x900x24" node scripts/perf/run.mjs --cold-only --runs 7 --out perf-results/f5-a1.json
  xvfb-run -a -s "-screen 0 1440x900x24" node scripts/perf/run.mjs --cold-only --runs 7 --out perf-results/f5-b1.json

Three rounds of each, alternating A and B; then `git apply -R` the patch and build again.

